      en: "The Slovnaft refinery in Bratislava is one of the most modern and highly complex oil processing facilities in Europe. Founded in 1946, it has become an indispensable part of Slovakia's energy infrastructure. The massive industrial complex in the southeastern part of the capital processes millions of tons of crude oil annually, most of which is imported via the Druzhba pipeline. Slovnaft produces not only high-quality fuels like gasoline and diesel but also a wide range of petrochemical products, including plastics and lubricants used across various industries. A significant portion of its production is destined for export to neighboring countries. In recent years, the company has invested heavily in environmental protection measures and new technologies to drastically reduce emissions and further increase operational efficiency.",
